From 1402ad95c4db48dd38140c62aea6bf916853f414 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Project <noreply@invalid>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 16:13:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 158/158] arm64: add dormant late-CPU startup arbitration

Add a C-only, generation-scoped state model for future P30 ownership. Require exact controller and target identities, serialize every transition and snapshot, retain operation-scoped one-shot history, drain an indivisible publisher, and make quarantine sticky and fail-closed.

Cover success retirement, CPU8-to-CPU9 reuse, cancellation and publication races, PREPARED/ABORTED/ARMED faults, K/C/P/E/U terminal rules, exact target mismatch, completion and online validation, and panic ordering with a default-off KUnit suite.

The model has no production caller, does not provide the future P24 owner or P30E MMU-off wire object, and leaves the MT6797 CPU boot and disable vetoes unchanged.

This experiment-only change has no certifying sign-off and is not submission-ready.
